INT. ROLLER DERBY RINK, LOCKER ROOM - EVENING

Rows of dented lockers. Skates on benches like sleeping animals. A banner on the wall: THE IRON MAIDENS OF MERIDIAN. The air smells of liniment and nerves.

BRYNHILDE "BRUISER" OKONKWO-LARSSON (30s, shoulders like a door, face paint half-applied) laces her skates with ferocious focus. Beside her, rookie JOSEFINA ABERNATHY-SILVA (19, stiff new helmet, wide eyes) copies every move. Across the room, coach HORTENSIA "HORTY" BELLAMY-OKORO (50s, whistle, tracksuit) leans against a locker with a clipboard.

HORTY
Ladies. Last bout of the season.

BRUISER
We know.

HORTY
Josefina, this is your first jam.

JOSEFINA
I know.

HORTY
You'll be nervous.

JOSEFINA
I'm not nervous.

BRUISER
She's nervous.

HORTY
Good. Nerves keep you alive.

She blows the whistle once, softly, as a kind of benediction. Bruiser stands, rolling her neck.

BRUISER
Come on, kid. Stay on my hip.

JOSEFINA
Where's your hip?

BRUISER
Wherever it is when you need it.

They stack fists. The crowd roars outside. A door bangs. The three women walk out together into a tunnel of light.
